From: zyi
Subject: [PATCH] rtla: poll on every commit, not at 50% buffer full

With the default buffer_percent (50), the tracer poll only wakes when
half the ring buffer is full. On a quiet system osnoise events trickle
in and never reach that, so rtla blocks in select() for minutes and
looks hung (this also explains the flaky osnoise/timerlat results on
the A733, see e902/doc/e902/FINDINGS-LEDGER.md T38). Poll on every
commit instead: zero cost here, rtla reads once per second anyway.

---
--- a/tools/tracing/rtla/src/trace.c
+++ b/tools/tracing/rtla/src/trace.c
@@ -171,6 +171,15 @@
 	if (!trace->inst)
 		goto out_err;
 
+	/*
+	 * The default buffer_percent (50) makes the tracer's poll wait
+	 * until half the ring buffer is full before waking readers. On a
+	 * quiet system osnoise events never reach that level, so rtla
+	 * blocks in select() for minutes and looks hung. Poll on every
+	 * commit instead.
+	 */
+	tracefs_instance_file_write(trace->inst, "buffer_percent", "0");
+
 	trace->tep = tracefs_local_events(NULL);
 	if (!trace->tep)
 		goto out_err;
